,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(2544.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-29\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(422,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(8138.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"5D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-5D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(8416.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(9176.2,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D459\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D459\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(331,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> is</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Tetraaquadiaminecobalt (III) chloride."},{"identifier":"B","content":"Tetraaquadiamminecobalt (III) chloride."},{"identifier":"C","content":"Diaminetetraaquacobalt (III) chloride."},{"identifier":"D","content":"Diamminetetraaquacobalt (III) chloride."}],"correct_options":["D"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>There are two ligands in the coordination entity, that is, ammine and aqua, but according to the IUPAC rule, alphabetical order is followed, that is, ammine is named first. Now calculating the oxidation state of Co, the net charge on the coordination entity is +3 as Cl has <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>1 and there are three Cl<sup><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></sup> outside the square brackets. So the oxidation state of Co will be III as both ammine and aqua are neutral ligands. So, its correct name will be diamminetetraaquacobalt (III) chloride.</p>"}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":180000,"topic":"nomenclature-of-coordination-compounds","type":"mcq","year":2012,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"yearKey":"iit-jee-2012-paper-1-offline","active":true},{"question_id":"1l23imyud","chapter":"p-block-elements","chapterGroup":"inorganic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-advanced","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en"],"marks":3,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"iit-jee-2012-paper-1-offline","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2012 Paper 1 Offline","permalink":"pwhich-ordering-of-compounds-is-according-to-the-decreasin-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-qazsqu3iyujckwym","question":{"en":{"direction":null,"content":"<p>Which ordering of compounds is according to the decreasing order of the oxidation state of nitrogen?</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"HNO<sub>3</sub>, NO, NH<sub>4</sub>Cl, N<sub>2</sub>"},{"identifier":"B","content":"HNO<sub>3</sub>, NO, N<sub>2</sub>, NH<sub>4</sub>Cl"},{"identifier":"C","content":"HNO<sub>3</sub>, NH<sub>4</sub>Cl, NO, N<sub>2</sub>"},{"identifier":"D","content":"NO, HNO<sub>3</sub>, NH<sub>4</sub>Cl, N<sub>2</sub>"}],"correct_options":["B"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>In HNO<sub>3</sub>, the oxidation state of N is +5 while in NO, it is +2. In N<sub>2</sub>, it is zero and in NH<sub>4</sub>Cl, the oxidation state of nitrogen is <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>3. So, the decreasing order of oxidation state of nitrogen is</p>\n<p>HNO<sub>3</sub> &gt; NO &gt; N<sub>2</sub> &gt; NH<sub>4</sub>Cl</p>"}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":180000,"topic":"group-15-elements-nitrogen-family","type":"mcq","year":2012,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"yearKey":"iit-jee-2012-paper-1-offline","active":true},{"question_id":"1l23irmod","chapter":"gaseous-state","chapterGroup":"physical-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"medium","exam":"jee-advanced","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en"],"marks":3,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"iit-jee-2012-paper-1-offline","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2012 Paper 1 Offline","permalink":"pfor-one-mole-of-a-van-der-waals-gas-when-b--0-and-t--30-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-qcq6zrgwkotyej6x","question":{"en":{"direction":null,"content":"<p>For one mole of a van der Waals gas when b = 0 and T = 300 K, the PV vs. 1/V plot is shown below. The value of the van der Waals constant a (atm L<sup>2</sup> mol<sup><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>2</sup>) is</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l24lf9pp/1b49bd1c-0106-4eef-940f-99088eea51e3/f7aac0e0-bf04-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24lf9pq.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l24lf9pp/1b49bd1c-0106-4eef-940f-99088eea51e3/f7aac0e0-bf04-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24lf9pq.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2012 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Gaseous State Question 10 English\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l24lf9pp/1b49bd1c-0106-4eef-940f-99088eea51e3/f7aac0e0-bf04-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24lf9pq.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l24lf9pp/1b49bd1c-0106-4eef-940f-99088eea51e3/f7aac0e0-bf04-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24lf9pq.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l24lf9pp/1b49bd1c-0106-4eef-940f-99088eea51e3/f7aac0e0-bf04-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24lf9pq.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l24lf9pp/1b49bd1c-0106-4eef-940f-99088eea51e3/f7aac0e0-bf04-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24lf9pq.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l24lf9pp/1b49bd1c-0106-4eef-940f-99088eea51e3/f7aac0e0-bf04-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24lf9pq.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l24lf9pp/1b49bd1c-0106-4eef-940f-99088eea51e3/f7aac0e0-bf04-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24lf9pq.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>","o